00:03:39.060 --> 00:04:03.660
<v Julia Sweeney>OK, so we're in the doctor's office, and Mike, who's doing really great and is responding really well to the treatment. But he's had so many spinal taps that they can't get into his spinal column anymore. So the doctor comes in. My dad's reading about the plague in India, because that's a good diversion. And my mom is looking at the doctors and saying, "Now, he looks single."
<v Julia Sweeney>好了，我们在医生办公室，迈克恢复得非常好，对治疗反应也很理想。但他做了太多次脊椎穿刺，医生已经没法再从他的脊椎柱进针了。医生进来了。我爸正在看关于印度瘟疫的书，因为这是一种很好的消遣。而我妈看着那些医生，说道：“看，那个医生好像单身。”

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:28.420
<v Julia Sweeney>And his doctor comes in. He says, "Michael, we can't get into your spinal column anymore, so we're thinking about putting a shunt in your head. And my brother goes, "What?" He goes, "A shunt?" And I go, "A shunt, like, an artificial opening to the brain." And Mike goes, "Well, where would this shunt be?" And the doctor goes, "Well, the best place we've found is to put it in the forehead."
<v Julia Sweeney>他的医生进来说：“迈克尔，我们无法再进入你的脊椎柱了，所以我们在考虑给你的脑部安装一个分流器。” 我哥问：“什么？” 他说：“分流器？” 我说：“分流器，就像通往大脑的人造开口。” 迈克问：“那这分流器会装在哪？” 医生说：“嗯，我们发现最好的位置是安装在前额。”

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:43.300
<v Julia Sweeney>And Mike goes, "If you think I am going to get a faucet put into my forehead. I'm already 90 pounds, and I have no hair. I'm not going to walk around for a year with a faucet sticking out of my forehead." And my mom goes, "No, I think it's more like a spigot."
<v Julia Sweeney>迈克说：“如果你觉得我会在额头上装个水龙头，那就大错特错了。我已经瘦到 90 磅了，头发也没了。我才不要带着个水龙头在额头上走上一年。” 我妈说：“不，我觉得那更像是一个水龙头开关（spigot）。”

