<v Terry Sweeney>I used to go to things like The Mine Shaft, which was in New York-- when I lived in New York-- which was much too hardcore for me. And people would be really dressed in these leather harnesses and leather caps and dog collars and totally done up. And I'd have tried to put on a black cardigan or something.
<v Terry Sweeney>我过去常去那种叫“矿井”（The Mine Shaft）的地方，在纽约——我住纽约的时候——那对我来说太硬核了。人们都穿着皮背带、皮帽、狗项圈，打扮得非常彻底。而我呢，总想套件黑色开衫之类的。

